<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 6.2 percent of their 1996/97 sunflower crop by February 14, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>However heavy recent rains in the south of Buenos Aires Province have damaged sunflower crops and humidity is helping the spready of sunflower fungus.</p>
<p>Maize sowing has reached 99.7 percent of intended sowing area, which at 3.8 billion hectares is 11.8 percent up on last year. But stunting Rio Cuarto virus has hit crops, especially west Buenos Aires, south Santa Fe and southwest Cordoba.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,814   99.7(100.0)    94.4    2.5   (0.4)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,412   99.7(100.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,039  100.0(100.0)   183f9    6.2   (2.0)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770   99.7(100.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	964  100.0  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>    ((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655))</p>
